
# NL-<issue> <Imperative summary>
#   <= 72 chars. Capital after the key. No colon after it. No trailing period.
#   NL-01 is the catch-all key for work that has no issue.
#
# Blank line, then a SHORT description of what the change makes true.
#
# HARD LIMIT: the whole message -- subject, body and Closes line together -- is
# 500 characters or fewer. Roughly five lines at 78 columns. Why the change is
# right, the alternative you rejected and the mutations you ran belong in the
# pull request body, not here.
#
# ASCII only: -- for an em dash, -> for an arrow.
#
# Review-response commit: first body line is
#   Closes #NN review thread <threadId>.
# Otherwise: Closes #NN as the last body line.
#
# NO trailers. No session links (claude.ai, Codex, Cursor or any other), no
# Co-authored-by bot lines, no generated-by footers.
#
# One idea per commit. A changed line that does not trace to the issue in the
# subject belongs in a different commit.
